1
00:00:03,206 --> 00:00:05,745
Every data team gets the same message every

2
00:00:05,745 --> 00:00:07,576
week: can you get me this data?

3
00:00:08,026 --> 00:00:10,401
This Fabric app puts every ask on one

4
00:00:10,401 --> 00:00:13,096
radar, ranked by a score anyone can check.

5
00:00:14,181 --> 00:00:17,448
The closer a blip sits to the centre, the higher

6
00:00:17,448 --> 00:00:21,191
it ranks. Its sector shows which team made the request.

7
00:00:21,641 --> 00:00:24,198
Size is supporters, and the trail behind

8
00:00:24,198 --> 00:00:26,051
it is how long it has waited.

9
00:00:26,501 --> 00:00:29,782
Hover a blip and the score explains itself:

10
00:00:29,782 --> 00:00:33,521
value, urgency and supporters, divided by effort.

11
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:37,306
Lenses repaint the same radar. Age shows who

12
00:00:37,306 --> 00:00:40,355
has waited longest; team shows who is asking.

13
00:00:42,442 --> 00:00:45,739
Today lists what needs the data team now. The

14
00:00:45,739 --> 00:00:49,622
blinking blips are requests still waiting for triage.

15
00:00:50,072 --> 00:00:53,209
One click flies the radar to the request

16
00:00:53,209 --> 00:00:56,502
and switches to the lens that explains it.

17
00:00:57,318 --> 00:01:00,868
Switch the view to a requester, and Today becomes

18
00:01:00,868 --> 00:01:03,838
where your own requests sit in the queue.

19
00:01:04,643 --> 00:01:08,043
Priya needs pipeline by region, so she files a flight plan.

20
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:12,503
As she types, similar open requests close in on the duplicate radar.

21
00:01:12,953 --> 00:01:17,313
She backs the existing request instead, and its score goes up.

22
00:01:18,113 --> 00:01:23,013
Back on the data team, the flight board shows every request by status.

23
00:01:23,463 --> 00:01:26,081
Move only offers what the rules allow,

24
00:01:26,081 --> 00:01:28,493
and triage asks for an effort size.

25
00:01:30,162 --> 00:01:33,209
Every request keeps a black box: how long it held

26
00:01:33,209 --> 00:01:36,442
each status, and an append-only log of who moved it.

27
00:01:37,242 --> 00:01:42,087
Requests, reasons and progress in one place, running on

28
00:01:42,087 --> 00:01:46,492
Fabric Apps in preview with a Fabric SQL database.
